# Frontend JavaScript Rules (MANDATORY)

## Minimal UI Patch
- Smallest possible diff: minimal DOM changes, minimal CSS changes.
- DO NOT redesign components unless asked.

## Date/Time
- Date MUST remain YYYY-MM-DD.
- Time MUST remain HH:MM.
- DO NOT rely on locale parsing for dates (no Date('15.12.2025') style).
- Always parse/format explicitly.

## Networking
- Handle fetch errors gracefully (timeouts if implemented, retry only if safe).
- DO NOT break existing API contracts (request/response shapes).
- If contract must change, keep backwards compatibility unless explicitly requested.

## Chat/Sockets
- Avoid double-initialization (no duplicate socket instances).
- Reconnect must not spam.
- Keep event handlers idempotent (avoid registering twice).

## CSP Compatibility
- Avoid inline scripts and inline event handlers if CSP is strict.
- Keep script imports and initialization consistent with project CSP policy.

## Finish Criteria
- Provide verification steps:
  - booking modal open → date select → slots render → confirm path
  - chat open → send/receive → no console errors
